er has raised about $297,000 with little outside help. An independent, Mark Davis, is on the ballot but running a minimal campaign.\n\nRaters across the board call the race Likely or Lean Republican, and prediction markets give Gruters roughly an 80 percent chance. A single August poll showed Kirschner up a point, but it is the only public survey and carries limited weight. Two local Republican officials crossing party lines to endorse Kirschner hint at modest slippage, and a Democratic-friendly national environment keeps the door open, but money and partisanship favor Gruters.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.257, "margin": -3.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2349, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1906, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2331, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1854, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1943, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2766, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2403, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2304, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1856, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2293, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2161, "margin": -5.5}]}